      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "「キャ」とターニャの叫び声が聞こえます。",
      "english_translation": "\"キャ!\" The sound of Tarnya's scream can be heard."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "「どうしたの？大丈夫？」私たちがいるのは、蓼科の森の中、ターニャの方を見ると長いシッポのキツネがターニャの叫び声に驚いたのか、立ち止まってじっとこちらを見ています。",
      "english_translation": "\"What's wrong? Are you okay?\" I looked at Tarnya, and saw that a fox with a long tail had stopped in the forest of Tateoka, apparently startled by her cries. It was standing still and staring intently at us."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "キツネ、ロシアにもいるでしょう？」一番多いのは鹿、親子の鹿が目の前に飛び出すことは珍しくありません。",
      "english_translation": "\"Are there also foxes in Russia?\" The most common animals are deer, and it's not uncommon to see a pair of parent and child deer appear suddenly."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "ウサギやいのしし、秋になるとドングリを落とす木のまわりにはリスがよく来ます。",
      "english_translation": "Rabbits, squirrels, and other animals often come around trees that drop acorns in the fall."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "「先生、熊はいませんよね？」と心配そうにターニャ。",
      "english_translation": "\"Teacher, there aren't any bears, right?\" Tanya asked anxiously."
    }
  ],
